hi there steve here again uh continuing  in this series  uh about the application of steve  covey's uh  very inspiring book seven habits of  highly effective people and how it  applies to language learning and his  fifth habit was what he calls you know  seek first to understand then  to be understood  and  this applies in life we should always  listen before talking hear what people  have to say  if we understand what they have to say  we can respond to it much better well  the same is true in language learning  and that's why  my whole approach to language learning  is so heavily input based  i want to understand i want to  understand the culture i want to  understand uh what people have to say i  want to feel confident that in any um  conversation  there won't be any big surprises i won't  find myself constantly saying i beg your  pardon a bigger pardon so that this  developing this  level of understanding is is key  uh then what we have to say is going to  make sense it's going to be a response  to what people said it's not just going  to be trotting out a few uh sentences  that we'll you know that we feel  confident uh in uttering it and it also  gets back to some of these other um  habits like the win-win in other words  any engagement you have with the  language if you are connecting with it  you're understanding you're listening  you're reading  all of this is a powerful win  so by having a  learning strategy that focuses on  understanding  uh you're guaranteeing yourself the  sense of win and achievement if on the  other hand you look at language learning  as a performance and then you're  constantly second guessing yourself and  oh i didn't speak as well as i would  like i wasn't able to express my  thoughts  i  struggled to find words  whereas when you are listening you're  constantly gaining you're constantly  learning listening and reading  understanding understanding not only the  language but understanding some aspect  of the culture so i i just find that  this emphasis on understanding the  language the culture on soaking it in  rather than  wanting to trot out the few sentences  that you can use  is is a much more long lasting  much more in the long run satisfying  way and it builds up a solid base from  which to develop your output skills so  seek first to understand  then to be understood  i think that applies to language  learning
 

